<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Stratji Mac entitlements — honest helper architecture vs production target.

  CURRENT (local-dev, this file):
  - App Sandbox is OFF. Flask :5050, Vinext :3000, content digest :3003 (osascript +
    Calendar/Podcasts SQLite), PDF helper :3002, Kite MCP :8080, launchd trampoline,
    and iCloud Health ZIP cannot all live inside one sandboxed UI process today.
  - Stratji.app is the AppKit + WKWebView shell. The data plane is sibling processes.
  - Full Disk Access may still be required for group-container SQLite until EventKit
    and user-selected folder bookmarks replace those reads.
  - TCC parent for helpers may still be Terminal / start-dashboard.command. Production
    should make Stratji.app the parent so Info.plist usage strings are what the user sees.

  PRODUCTION TARGET (not this file yet):
  - Sandboxed Stratji.app (network client, Apple Events, user-selected files).
  - Separate notarized XPC / launchd helper for Flask, Vinext, digest, Kite, Health ZIP.
  - Do not copy InvestmentDashboard.entitlements (sandboxed WebView client) onto Stratji.app.
  - Do not add Camera, Microphone, Contacts, Bluetooth, Location, or Accessibility.

  Permissions the product actually uses:
  - network.client — loopback dashboard + Kite/yfinance/NSE/Tailscale HTTPS
  - automation.apple-events — Mail, Reminders, Notes, Podcasts
  - Calendar / Reminders / HealthKit — declared in Info.plist usage strings; HealthKit
    entitlement stays on the iOS target until the Mac binary imports HealthKit
  - com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars / reminders — EventKit full-access
    prompts from Stratji Settings Connect (unsandboxed; usage strings still required)
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<false/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.personal-information.reminders</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
